WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:05.360
Jax Teller's Shakespearian tragedy ends&nbsp;
in predictably catastrophic style on "Sons&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:10.240
of Anarchy." This is Jax's rocky road&nbsp;
from acting as vice president of SAMCRO&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:15.920
to enacting revenge upon his stepfather, Clay, and&nbsp;
his own mother, Gemma, for his father's murder.

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:21.600
Jax's father, John Teller, was an idealist,&nbsp;
Vietnam vet, and founding member of the Sons.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:26.240
He hoped that the Charming, California biker club&nbsp;
would have a positive influence on the world.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:30.240
After losing his youngest son, Jax's&nbsp;
little brother Thomas, to a heart defect,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:35.120
he fell into a deep depression and began putting&nbsp;
the history of the club down in his memoir.

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:37.840
While John was constantly&nbsp;
running off with his mistress,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:41.840
Gemma was left to deal with Thomas'&nbsp;
illness and subsequent passing alone.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:46.640
She agreed to help Clay put an end to John in&nbsp;
a staged road accident. Clay quickly became&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:52.080
club president and began entangling the club&nbsp;
deeper with other organized criminal elements.

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:53.440
And that's just the backstory!

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:59.360
Jax is in turmoil when the show opens. The&nbsp;
club's warehouse is mysteriously burned down.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:04.400
On the same day, his pregnant ex-wife Wendy&nbsp;
overdoses on heroin and is rushed to the hospital&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:09.120
where Jax discovers his high school sweetheart,&nbsp;
Tara, will be one of his child's surgeons.

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:11.840
"I want to help your son."

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:14.480
"His name is Abel"

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:20.000
Abel Teller is delivered via c-section and,&nbsp;
thanks to Tara's surgical intervention,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:25.200
beats the two-to-one odds against his survival.&nbsp;
Tara and Jax, reunited for the first time since&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:29.840
high school, begin to fall into a relationship&nbsp;
in spite of themselves. While looking for baby&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:34.960
clothing for Abel, Jax finds his father's writings&nbsp;
in a storage crate and becomes inspired by the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:39.680
old man's vision for SAMCRO, which the club&nbsp;
is decidedly not living up to under Clay.

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:44.240
The Sons ultimately find themselves divided&nbsp;
when Donna, the wife of Jax's best friend and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:49.360
trusted lieutenant, Opie, is accidentally&nbsp;
killed by Tig, Clay's Sergeant at Arms.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:53.840
The bullet was intended for Opie, whom Clay&nbsp;
falsely believes is informing on the Sons&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:58.520
thanks to information planted by June Stahl,&nbsp;
an ATF agent trying to take down the Sons.

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:03.760
SAMCRO soon finds themselves in a turf war&nbsp;
with the League of American Nationalists,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:08.320
a militant white supremacist group. As&nbsp;
Clay and Jax vie for control of the club,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:14.080
Gemma is kidnapped, beaten, and sexually assaulted&nbsp;
by the League. United by a desire for vengeance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:18.160
Clay and Jax combine forces to remove&nbsp;
the Nazis from Charming for good.

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:21.840
"How do you want to handle it?"

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:23.840
"We kill them all."

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:28.960
Just as the coast seems clear, Jax learns that&nbsp;
Abel has been kidnapped by the head of the True&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:33.840
Irish Republican Army, who believes that Gemma&nbsp;
is involved with the death of his son. Jax and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:38.880
the Sons head to Belfast to recover the boy,&nbsp;
where Jax meets his father's mistress, Maureen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:42.240
who gives him more of his father's&nbsp;
letters to add to his collection.

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:46.160
After Jax returns home, Agent Stahl&nbsp;
offers him legal immunity for Gemma&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:51.120
and lighter sentences for the Sons if he turns&nbsp;
on them. Upon learning that Tara is pregnant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:54.880
Jax takes the deal. Stahl informs&nbsp;
the club of their negotiations,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:59.760
but instead of turning on Jax, Opie takes&nbsp;
out Stahl, avenging his wife's death.

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:03.840
Jax soon learns that Stahl has set them&nbsp;
up, and the club ends up in prison.

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:08.000
After a 14-month prison sentence,&nbsp;
Jax and the gang are released.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:11.360
Jax plans on exiting the club and&nbsp;
making a better life for himself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:15.440
Tara, and his children, but gets&nbsp;
drawn even deeper into club business.

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:19.040
Gemma discovers Maureen's letters&nbsp;
from John among Jax's things,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:24.560
detailing his suspicion that Gemma and Clay were&nbsp;
conspiring to kill him. Clay kills multiple people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:30.000
to suppress the truth — including Opie's father.&nbsp;
Clay and Gemma begin to come apart at the seams,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:35.120
their relationship exploding after a particularly&nbsp;
ugly fight. Gemma has the letters altered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:39.760
to remove proof of her involvement in John's&nbsp;
death, then informs Jax that Clay arranged his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:45.600
father's murder. Clay gets voted out of the club&nbsp;
presidency, with Jax assuming control of the Sons.

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:50.160
The club soon runs afoul of a gang seeking revenge&nbsp;
after Tig killed the daughter of their leader,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:55.680
Damon Pope. Tara and Jax finally marry, and&nbsp;
the Sons find themselves imprisoned once again.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.680 --> 00:04:00.080
To pay off their debt to Pope, they're forced to&nbsp;
trade the life of one of their imprisoned members.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:05.120
Opie volunteers, and is brutally beaten to death&nbsp;
in one of the series' most gruesome scenes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:07.680
Jax later kills Pope and pins the hit on Clay.

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:12.000
After a gun connected to the Sons&nbsp;
is used in a school shooting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:17.200
Jax decides to get out of their IRA-related gun&nbsp;
trade, but Clay — imprisoned for the murder of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:21.840
Pope — relies on the IRA, and a few of his&nbsp;
SAMCRO buddies to break him out of prison.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:26.800
The resulting mess concludes with Jax finally&nbsp;
shooting Clay to death and pinning it on the IRA.

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:27.940
"Fair enough"

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:32.080
Tara is given the chance to turn&nbsp;
state's evidence against the Sons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:36.400
and Gemma believes she's already turned on&nbsp;
them. Though Jax and Tara have reconciled,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:40.560
Gemma takes it upon herself to protect&nbsp;
her son. She stabs Tara to death,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:45.040
and absconds before she's discovered,&nbsp;
leaving Jax alone to find his wife and mourn.

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:49.680
With nothing left to lose and the love of&nbsp;
his life now gone, Jax goes on a roaring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:54.240
rampage of revenge, eventually catching&nbsp;
up with Gemma at her father's house.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:58.800
He kills his mother in her garden, entering&nbsp;
a dark place from which he can't return.

00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:04.080
Jax says goodbye to his sons and entrusts them to&nbsp;
Wendy. He also gives Wendy all of his possessions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:08.960
and instructs her to take the boys and leave&nbsp;
Charming, ensuring they won't grow up in the Club.

00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:11.680
"I need my sons to grow up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:17.760
hating the thought of me."

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:21.920
He leaves his club ring at Opie's&nbsp;
grave and kisses Tara's headstone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:25.840
before visiting the place where his&nbsp;
father died, announcing his forgiveness.

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:29.200
Leading the police on a chase down the&nbsp;
same highway where his father died,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:34.240
Jax drives his motorcycle head-on into a semi&nbsp;
truck, ending his life in the same place and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.240 --> 00:05:39.280
in the same way his father died years ago. Just&nbsp;
like the ending of "Hamlet," it's a bloodbath.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:43.520
Unlike the ending of "Hamlet," however, two&nbsp;
small boys get a chance at a peaceful life.

